{
  "case_id": "2021-21-499",
  "document_hash": "ec32c9c02a71487021e6307322393f7033cae138a897d306c871d9914b723a1f",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec32c9c02a71487021e6307322393f7033cae138a897d306c871d9914b723a1f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec32c9c02a71-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:00 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec32c9c02a71487021e6307322393f7033cae138a897d306c871d9914b723a1f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec32c9c02a71-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Ninth Circuit's extension of Miranda into 1983 litigation is inconsistent with settled precedent and sound policy. For two reasons, you should reverse."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec32c9c02a71487021e6307322393f7033cae138a897d306c871d9914b723a1f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec32c9c02a71-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Second, as Tekoh now concedes, the Ninth Circuit's proximate causation holding is wrong. That concession provides a complete basis for reversal here. Officers can't be held liable when the mistakes are made by prosecutors and judges."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec32c9c02a71487021e6307322393f7033cae138a897d306c871d9914b723a1f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec32c9c02a71-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Mr. Martinez, the -- in -- in Dickerson, we held -- the Court held that Miranda could not be displaced by a federal statute by Congress."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec32c9c02a71487021e6307322393f7033cae138a897d306c871d9914b723a1f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec32c9c02a71-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Mr. Martinez, if I could focus just for a minute on the language of the cause of action here, 1983. It gives individuals a right against the \"deprivation of any rights, privileges, or immunities secured by the Constitution and laws.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec32c9c02a71487021e6307322393f7033cae138a897d306c871d9914b723a1f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec32c9c02a71-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Certainly."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec32c9c02a71487021e6307322393f7033cae138a897d306c871d9914b723a1f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec32c9c02a71-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: That -- that if we come out your way, it will undermine Dickerson, it will be understood as inconsistent with Dickerson. I mean, that's what I think, and I know you don't think it, but I want to put that aside and -- and -- and to have you at least acknowledge that there are many people who will think of this as utterly inconsistent with Dickerson."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec32c9c02a71487021e6307322393f7033cae138a897d306c871d9914b723a1f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec32c9c02a71-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: What if the police officer purposely lies in order to convince the prosecutor to use the statement?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec32c9c02a71487021e6307322393f7033cae138a897d306c871d9914b723a1f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec32c9c02a71-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Counsel, I -- I'm not sure what witness immunity has to do with this issue. Yes, you're immune from prosecution for any testimony you give at a trial. But, if you're testifying falsely and that's what induces a judge or a prosecutor to use your statement, I -- I don't understand why that should be immune from 1983."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec32c9c02a71487021e6307322393f7033cae138a897d306c871d9914b723a1f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec32c9c02a71-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I get that argument.\nBut there's an additional quantum of harm surely\nassociated with its introduction at trial and a\npotential conviction wrongfully. And your rule,\nI think, would take that out of play, and maybe\nit won't, but I'd like to hear your thoughts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Suri",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec32c9c02a71487021e6307322393f7033cae138a897d306c871d9914b723a1f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec32c9c02a71-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the appropriate forum for redressing harms that occur in the trial itself is the appeal process in habeas corpus, not a collateral civil suit attacking the trial ruling."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Suri",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec32c9c02a71487021e6307322393f7033cae138a897d306c871d9914b723a1f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec32c9c02a71-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We think Miranda is a constitutional right. To use the language of Section 1983, it is any right, privilege, or immunity secured by the Constitution."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec32c9c02a71487021e6307322393f7033cae138a897d306c871d9914b723a1f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec32c9c02a71-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the trials that we've had in this so far, have there been any findings by the jury that the officer lied?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hoffman",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec32c9c02a71487021e6307322393f7033cae138a897d306c871d9914b723a1f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec32c9c02a71-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We didn't make that statement in that way because both sides were operating under Ninth Circuit precedent, which didn't require you to make that statement. We didn't elevate the standard for proximate cause on our own."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hoffman",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec32c9c02a71487021e6307322393f7033cae138a897d306c871d9914b723a1f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec32c9c02a71-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The reports omit the true circumstances of the interrogation, make it seem like a completely voluntary statement and that he confessed willingly, and don't say anything about the fact that there's an hour-long interrogation in a closed room with threats and -- and all the rest that would make it clearly a custodial interrogation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec32c9c02a71487021e6307322393f7033cae138a897d306c871d9914b723a1f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec32c9c02a71-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can you say to us right now that you have some evidence you would like to introduce that the policeman did mislead the prosecutor about what happened, other than the policeman speaking as a witness?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hoffman",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec32c9c02a71487021e6307322393f7033cae138a897d306c871d9914b723a1f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec32c9c02a71-0003-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If Miranda's violated, the violation has to be of the Fifth Amendment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec32c9c02a71487021e6307322393f7033cae138a897d306c871d9914b723a1f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec32c9c02a71-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why isn't that the right way to think about that case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hoffman",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec32c9c02a71487021e6307322393f7033cae138a897d306c871d9914b723a1f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec32c9c02a71-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "His life was destroyed by these actions. He gets acquitted. When the full story comes out, he is contending that the officer set him up for this and basically set up the prosecutor and the -- and the court too. What remedy does he have? That's what Section 1983 is for."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec32c9c02a71487021e6307322393f7033cae138a897d306c871d9914b723a1f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec32c9c02a71-0003-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 83,
        "start": 83
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 11:21 a.m., the case was submitted.)"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
